('K-4','Freeze the Convert contracts','Start','Turn the draft endpoints in contracts/src/convert.ts into real Zod schemas: params, query, body, response and permission for every Convert endpoint, plus fixtures. The other three build against these from 27 November, so after the freeze a change is its own merge request reviewed by everyone.','As Developer 4 I publish exact request and response shapes for Convert, so that the frontend, the backend and the other stages can build in parallel without guessing.','Contracts','dev4',2,true,array['G-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4, §5','docs/stages/CONVERT.md','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §5, §15.8']::text[],array['contracts/src/convert.ts','contracts/src/fixtures/*']::text[],array[]::text[],array['pnpm verify passes with no draft contract left in your file','The contract coverage test shows every endpoint registered (stub or real)','Reviewed and approved by the other three developers before 27 November']::text[],array['Replace every z.unknown() placeholder in your contract file with a real schema; mark nothing as draft','Each stub route keeps answering 501 but now with the frozen schema, so callers type-check','Add fixtures (invented data only) next to the contract for tests and frontend mocks']::text[],array['Check every screen from your stage audit maps to at least one contract','Build one screen against the frozen contract with fixture data to prove the shapes are usable']::text[],array['Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Routes only through defineRoute with a contract and a permission']::text[],array['Which fields are optional, and why? Every optional field is a branch someone must test','Which response fields could leak data a role should not see?','Which of your endpoints are public, and what stops them being abused?']::text[],2041),
('Q-01','Intake rules: outcome and conditions from the answers','Qualify','A pure function that takes the ten rule answers and returns the proposed outcome (Go, Conditional go, No-go), the state of each condition (Met, Open with its code and what to do, Stop with its reason and way back) and the Gate A rule state. Everything else in Qualify shows or stores what this function says, so it must be right and fully tested.','As an Immersion lead I see an outcome worked out the same way every time from the customer''s answers, so that I decide on facts and not on a feeling.','Intake','dev1',2,true,array['K-1']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (conditions check)','docs/blueprint/rules/intake.v1.yaml','docs/blueprint/SPEC.md §5.1','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (Gate A pass_rule)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/rules.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/rules.test.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/intake-rules.ts (YAML loader)']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A table-driven test covers every option of every question (at least 27 rows)','All go gives Go and "10 of 10 conditions met"','Any stop gives No-go even when other answers are conditions','q04 answered cond gives Conditional go with C4 "Ask the customer''s IT team which AI tool is approved for company data"','Gate A rule state changes to pass when C2, C3, C6, C7 and C10 are closed']::text[],array['rules.ts: evaluateIntake(answers, rulesVersion) using the worst-answer rule from intake.v1.yaml (any stop means No-go; else any condition means Conditional go; else Go)','Load intake.v1.yaml once at start, validate it with Zod, keep the version string on every result','gateARuleState(): pass only when q02, q03, q06, q07 and q10 are go or their conditions are closed','No database, no I/O: rules only']::text[],array['None in this task (Q-06 shows the result)']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place']::text[],array['What should happen if the rules file has a question the form does not, or the other way round?','Why must the rules version be stored with each result?','How will you prove the option text shown to people is exactly the text in the YAML?']::text[],2112),
('Q-02','Form builder: rule questions and custom questions','Qualify','Inside a client card the Immersion lead creates an intake form. It always starts with the ten rule questions; the lead may reword help text, reorder, and add custom questions of six types. Rule questions cannot be removed because each one feeds a condition.','As an Immersion lead I build the intake form for this customer in a few minutes, so that I get the answers I need without a call.','Intake','dev1',3,true,array['Q-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (form builder)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 points 1 and 4','docs/blueprint/prototype/app-flow-map.html (Qualify, Edit form)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/routes.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/repo.ts','backend/src/db/schema/intake.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/FormBuilderPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/qualify/QuestionEditor.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/forms','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/forms','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId','PATCH /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId']::text[],array['A new form has exactly the ten rule questions in rules order','Removing a rule question is refused with 400 and a clear message','An Immersion team member gets 403 on every builder write and sees the builder read-only','Two leads editing at once: the second save gets 412 and is asked to reload']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/forms creates a Draft form with version 1 holding the ten rule questions','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/forms and GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId','PATCH /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId edits help text, order and custom questions (single choice, multiple choice, short text, long text, date, number)','Tables intake_forms and form_versions (questions as JSON validated by Zod)','Events FormCreated and FormEdited (no question text in the event)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/qualify/FormBuilderPage.tsx at /w/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/forms/:formId/edit','Question list with drag or up and down buttons, add question dialog, rule questions marked with a lock and "Feeds condition C4"','States: loading, saving, saved, error with retry, conflict (someone else saved)']::text[],array['Routes only through defineRoute with a contract and a permission','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['How do you stop a custom question pretending to be a rule question?','What is the smallest data shape for a question that covers all six types?','What should the lead see when the form changes under them?']::text[],3113),
('Q-03','Form states and versions: draft, live, paused, closed, archived','Qualify','A form moves through Draft, Live, Paused, Closed and Archived, and each state allows only certain changes (the table in PHASE1_PLAN §15.5). Changing a rule question on a Live form saves a new version, and every response keeps the version it was filled on.','As an Immersion lead I can open, pause and close my form safely, so that a customer never fills in a half-edited form and old answers keep their meaning.','Intake','dev1',3,false,array['Q-02']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (form states)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 point 4 (state table)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.10 scenarios 4 and 5']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/rules.ts (form transitions)','backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/FormList.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/state','DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId']::text[],array['A Live form cannot be deleted (409 with the reason)','A Draft form with no responses can be deleted','Editing a Live form''s rule question saves version 2; an earlier response keeps version 1','A Closed form refuses every edit','Every transition not in the table is refused and writes nothing']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/state with the target state; a transition table in rules.ts decides what is allowed','DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId only in Draft with no responses','Editing a Live or Paused form: custom wording only in place; any other change creates form_versions row n+1','Events FormStateChanged and FormVersionCreated']::text[],array['State chip and the allowed buttons only (Enable, Pause, Close, Archive, Delete) on the form list in the Qualify tab','Confirm dialog for Close and Delete that says what will happen','Paused and Closed forms show why the customer cannot open them']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Write the full transition table first. Which transitions are missing from the plan?','What happens to an open customer session when the form is paused?','How will the archived form stay available for the retention period but out of the list?']::text[],3114),
('Q-04','Form password and share link','Qualify','The lead sets a form password (12 characters or more), an optional open and close date, and how many responses are allowed. "Copy link" gives /f/{token}. The app never emails the password; the lead sends link and password by two different channels.','As an Immersion lead I share a protected link with the customer, so that only the people I gave the password to can answer.','Intake','dev1',4,false,array['Q-03']::text[],array['Step-up check from core/auth.ts: until Developer 2 lands step-up (A-08) the guard is a stub that passes in development']::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (share the form)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 points 2 and 3','GUARDRAILS.md (secrets and tokens)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/repo.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/SharePanel.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/password']::text[],array['A password under 12 characters is refused','The password and the raw token never appear in a response body after creation, in logs or in events','Changing the password ends customer sessions opened with the old one','An Immersion team member cannot change the password (403)']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/password: Argon2id hash (core/password.ts), step-up required, ends open customer sessions','form_links table: random token from core/tokens.ts, only its hash stored, open and close dates, response limit','Changing the password writes FormPasswordChanged (never the password)']::text[],array['Share panel in the Qualify tab: password field with strength hint, dates, response limit, Copy link button','A clear line: "Send the link and the password through two different channels"','No customer name field anywhere in the share flow']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Where could the raw token leak (logs, referrer header, analytics) and how do you stop each one?','Why is the token stored as a hash, and how do you look it up quickly?','What does the lead do if they lose the password?']::text[],4115),
('Q-05','Customer form: unlock, answer and submit','Qualify','The public page /f/{token}. The customer enters the form password and "Your name" (any name or role title, so the lead knows who sent it), answers the questions, and submits. Five wrong passwords lock the link for 15 minutes and notify the lead. The page shows nothing else about the deal.','As a customer contact I answer the intake questions on my own time without an account, so that TCS can prepare a session that fits us.','Intake','dev1',4,true,array['Q-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (customer form)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 point 5','docs/blueprint/acceptance/phase1.feature (Intake through a form link)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/public-routes.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','backend/src/db/schema/intake.ts (pii.form_submitters)','frontend/src/features/public-form/FormPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/public-form/ThankYou.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/f/:token','POST /api/f/:token/unlock','POST /api/f/:token/responses']::text[],array['5 wrong passwords lock the link for 15 minutes and notify the lead','Unknown, paused and closed tokens give the same kind of answer (no hint which tokens exist)','submittedBy is stored only in pii.form_submitters and shown only to the Immersion lead and team','The page works on a phone at 360 pixels wide']::text[],array['Public routes GET /api/f/:token, POST /api/f/:token/unlock, POST /api/f/:token/responses (no account, own rate limits)','Unlock checks the Argon2id hash, counts failures per link, locks for 15 minutes after 5 and writes FormLocked (lead notified through the action or mail stub)','Unlock gives a short-lived form session cookie scoped to /api/f/:token','Response stored with its form version; submittedBy stored in pii.form_submitters, linked by id','Respects open and close dates, paused state and response limit']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/public-form/FormPage.tsx at /f/:token: password and "Your name", then the questions, then Submit','The line "In your answers, use role titles. Do not name other people"','Thank you page: "Thank you. TCS will be in touch." and nothing else','States: paused, closed, locked (with the time left), wrong password, network error, already submitted']::text[],array['Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['What can an attacker learn from timing or error text on the public page, and how do you make all failures look alike?','How is the form session cookie different from a staff session cookie?','What happens if the customer submits twice or loses connection on Submit?']::text[],4116),
('Q-06','Names check on free-text answers','Qualify','Free text from customers must not carry personal names. A shared check flags likely names (capitalised first and last name pairs, email addresses, phone numbers, "Mr", "Ms" and similar) before submit, and the customer is asked to use role titles. Other stages call the same check through the intake module''s index.ts.','As a customer contact I am warned before I type a colleague''s name, so that the deal record keeps role titles only.','Intake','dev1',4,false,array['Q-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (names check)','docs/blueprint/SPEC.md (names scan, role titles)','docs/blueprint/rules/intake.v1.yaml (record_fields_note)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/rules.ts (namesCheck)','backend/src/modules/intake/names.test.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/index.ts','frontend/src/features/public-form/NameWarning.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A table-driven test with at least 30 rows: names, role titles, emails, phone numbers, company names that look like names','"Head of Finance" and "Customer A" pass; "Anna Berg" and "anna.berg@example.com" are flagged','A flagged answer is not stored']::text[],array['rules.ts: namesCheck(text) returns flagged spans with a reason; pure function','Called on POST /api/f/:token/responses: flagged answers are refused with 422 and the spans','Exported from backend/src/modules/intake/index.ts for Prepare and Convert to reuse']::text[],array['Inline warning under the field with the flagged words highlighted and "Use a role title, for example Head of Finance"','Frontend check is a hint only; the backend decides']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','The frontend hides what a role cannot do, but the backend still refuses it']::text[],array['What false positives will annoy customers (product names, cities) and how will you allow them?','Why must the check run on the server even if the page already ran it?','Who else in the team will call this, and what shape do they need back?']::text[],4117),
('Q-07','Responses list and Send to Qualify','Qualify','The Qualify tab lists responses: who sent it, when, the form version and the status New, Reviewed, Sent to Qualify. The lead presses Send to Qualify, which creates the intake from the answers, runs the rules, and gives the lead "Confirm the intake outcome".','As an Immersion lead I pick the response I trust and send it to Qualify, so that the conditions are worked out without me copying anything.','Intake','dev1',5,true,array['Q-05','Q-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (responses, send to Qualify)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 point 6, §6','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.10 scenario 7']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','backend/src/modules/intake/repo.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/ResponsesSection.tsx','frontend/src/features/qualify/ResponseView.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/responses','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/responses/:responseId/send-to-qualify']::text[],array['Send to Qualify writes IntakeSubmitted and IntakeOutcomeProposed in one transaction','Pressing it twice (or two leads at once) creates one intake, not two','Immersion team can read responses but gets 403 on Send to Qualify','A Research analyst gets 404 on the responses route']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/forms/:formId/responses (lead and team), POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/responses/:responseId/send-to-qualify (lead)','One transaction: intakes row with the rule result and rules version, response status Sent to Qualify, events IntakeSubmitted and IntakeOutcomeProposed','The confirm_intake action is created by the actions engine from IntakeSubmitted (C-02)','Sending a second response replaces the open proposal only before it is confirmed']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/qualify/ResponsesSection.tsx in the Qualify tab: table with status chips, open a response read-only, Mark reviewed, Send to Qualify with a confirm','Empty state: "No responses yet. Share the form link with the customer."']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What happens if two leads press Send to Qualify at once? Which database constraint makes it safe?','What should happen to an already confirmed intake if a new response arrives?','Which response fields may the Immersion team see?']::text[],5118),
('Q-08','Conditions check in the Qualify tab','Qualify','The Qualify tab shows the ten intake conditions, not the questions. Each reads Met, Open (code and what to do, for example "C4 · Ask the customer''s IT team which AI tool is approved") or Stop (reason and way back). Above the list: the proposed outcome and "8 of 10 conditions met".','As an Immersion lead I see at a glance what is ready and what is open, so that I know what to chase before the session.','Intake','dev1',5,false,array['Q-07']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (conditions check)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.5 point 7','docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (intake confirm)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/routes.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/QualifyTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/qualify/ConditionList.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify']::text[],array['The tab never lists question text','Counts match the rules function for the stored answers','A Stop shows its way back text','The page passes axe and reads well on a phone']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify returns the outcome, the ten conditions with state, closure info and the Gate A rule state','Reads the stored intake result; never recomputes with a newer rules version silently']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/qualify/QualifyTab.tsx: outcome banner, "x of 10 conditions met", conditions list with Met, Open and Stop styles','Before any intake: the form list and responses only, with a short explanation','Immersion team: same view, no action buttons']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The frontend hides what a role cannot do, but the backend still refuses it','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['How will a colour-blind user tell Met, Open and Stop apart?','What should the tab show for a No-go?','What exactly changes on screen when a condition is closed by someone else (live update)?']::text[],5119),
('Q-09','Confirm the intake outcome and Gate A','Qualify','The lead confirms the proposed outcome or changes it with a written reason, which records Gate A. When Gate A passes the client moves to Prepare and the Research analyst is asked to prepare the context pack. A No-go closes the client with a check-in date.','As an Immersion lead I record the Gate A decision in one step with my reason, so that preparation starts at once and the log shows why.','Intake','dev1',6,true,array['Q-08']::text[],array['Step-up stub until A-08 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (Gate A)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (confirm_intake, propose_gate_a, confirm_gate_a)','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml (combine, evidence_ref_required)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (A)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/ConfirmOutcomeDialog.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/confirm']::text[],array['Changing the outcome without a reason is refused','Gate A passed moves the client to Prepare and writes the events in one transaction','Without a fresh step-up the call gets 401 step_up_required and writes nothing','A second confirm on the same intake is refused (409)']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/confirm with outcome, reason (required if different from the proposal) and evidence reference','Step-up required; one transaction: IntakeOutcomeConfirmed, then Gate A through the core decision service (gate_decisions), then advanceStage to prepare when passed','Phase 1 combines propose_gate_a and confirm_gate_a into one action "Record Gate A" (roles.p1.yaml combine)','Creates close_condition actions for open conditions (through events)']::text[],array['Confirm dialog: proposed outcome, choice of outcome, reason field that appears when it differs, evidence reference field','After confirm: the stage rail highlights Prepare and the live log shows the decision sentence']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','Other modules are used only through their index.ts']::text[],array['Which events must be written, and in what order, for the actions engine to create the right next actions?','What does the log sentence say when a stand-in records for the sponsor?','What can still be undone after Gate A, and by whom?']::text[],6110),
('Q-10','Close conditions and the conditional go exception','Qualify','Each open condition gets "Mark closed" with a short note. When all Gate A conditions are closed the log says "Gate A criteria are now met". A Conditional go needs a recorded exception (facts, commitments with owner role and date, review date) and an approval reference before the client leaves Qualify.','As an Immersion lead I close conditions as I clear them and record an exception when we go ahead anyway, so that nobody runs a session on hidden risks.','Intake','dev1',6,false,array['Q-09']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (conditions, exception)','docs/blueprint/rules/intake.v1.yaml (conditions, exception)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (record_exception, approve_exception, close_condition)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/intake/service.ts','frontend/src/features/qualify/CloseConditionButton.tsx','frontend/src/features/qualify/ExceptionForm.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/conditions/:code/close','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/exception']::text[],array['Closing C2, C3, C6, C7 and C10 makes the Gate A rule state pass and writes the log line once','An exception without commitments or review date is refused','Closing an already closed condition is refused and writes nothing','Stop conditions cannot be marked closed']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/conditions/:code/close','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/qualify/exception (record and approve in one step in Phase 1, approval reference required)','Tables condition_closures and intake_exceptions; events ConditionClosed, ExceptionRecorded, ExceptionApproved','Gate A rule state recomputed from closures']::text[],array['"Mark closed" on each open condition with a note field','Exception form with the three required fields and the approval reference; read-only summary after approval']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Who owns each condition in Phase 1 (roles.p1.yaml stand-ins), and how do you show it?','Why must commitments use role titles, and how do you check it?','What should happen if a condition is closed after Gate A was confirmed as Conditional go?']::text[],6111),
('P-01','Context pack editor for the Research analyst','Prepare','When Gate A passes, the Research analyst gets "Prepare the context pack" on Today. The pack has a company profile, the sponsor''s priorities, challenge cards and sourced claims. The analyst edits it in the Prepare tab and it saves as they go.','As a Research analyst I build the context pack in one place inside the client card, so that the session material rests on checked facts.','Prep','dev2',5,true,array['K-2']::text[],array['A client already in Prepare from the seed data until Q-09 moves clients there for real','Names check from the intake module index.ts (stub that passes until Q-06 lands)']::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (context pack)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.6 points 1 and 2','docs/blueprint/SPEC.md §4.4']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/routes.ts','backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','backend/src/modules/prep/repo.ts','backend/src/db/schema/prep.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/PrepareTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/prepare/ContextPackEditor.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack','PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack']::text[],array['Only the Research analyst can edit; lead, team and consultant see it read-only','A stale save gets 412 and keeps the analyst''s text on screen','The names check (intake module) runs on free text and blocks personal names','Editing is refused once the pack is approved']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack and PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack (prep.edit, If-Match version)','Tables context_packs and cards; pack status Draft, In review, Returned, Approved','Starts empty when the client enters Prepare (listens for the stage change through the clients module index.ts)','Event ContextPackSaved (no content in the event)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/prepare/ContextPackEditor.tsx in the Prepare tab: sections Profile, Priorities, Challenge cards, Claims','Autosave with "Saved" and "Could not save, retry" states; conflict message when someone else saved','Locked read-only view when the pack is in review or approved']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['How do you autosave without losing text when two tabs are open?','Which parts of the pack become session material later, and in what shape does Developer 3 need them?','How will the analyst know a priority came from the intake answers?']::text[],5222),
('P-02','Claims, sources and flagged claims','Prepare','Every figure or fact in the pack is a claim with a source (title, link or document reference, date checked). Claims can be flagged when unsure; all flags must be resolved before H2. This is what makes "every on-screen figure opened at its source" true.','As a Research analyst I attach a source to every claim and clear every flag, so that no number in the session is made up.','Prep','dev2',6,false,array['P-01']::text[],array['Storage adapter stub that stores files in memory until F-03 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (claims)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (H2 checklist)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/ClaimsList.tsx','frontend/src/features/prepare/ResolveClaimDialog.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/claims/:claimId/resolve']::text[],array['A claim without a source cannot be saved','A non-https link is refused','Resolving writes ClaimResolved once and clears the flag count','Only the analyst can resolve']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/claims/:claimId/resolve','Table claims: text, source, checked date, flagged, resolution note','Links must be https; file sources go through the storage adapter (Developer 4) with a stub until it lands','Events ClaimFlagged, ClaimResolved']::text[],array['Claims list with source chips, a Flag button and a Resolve dialog','Filter "Flagged only", count of open flags in the Prepare tab header']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What counts as a source, and what is not good enough?','How do you keep a claim and the card that uses it in step when either changes?','What does the lead need to see about claims during review?']::text[],6223),
('P-03','Send for review (H2), approve or return','Prepare','The analyst signs H2 (facts signed) and presses Send for review. The lead reviews and either approves or returns the pack with comments. A returned pack goes back to the analyst with the comments shown beside the sections.','As an Immersion lead I review the pack and approve it or send it back with clear comments, so that the material is right before anyone sees it.','Prep','dev2',6,true,array['P-02']::text[],array['Step-up stub until A-08 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (review and return)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.6 points 2 and 3','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (resolve_flags_sign_h2)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/ReviewPanel.tsx','frontend/src/features/prepare/SubmitForReview.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/submit','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/review']::text[],array['Submit with an open flag is refused and lists the flags','Return without a comment is refused','The return and resubmit loop can run more than once and the log shows each round','Only the lead can review (403 for others, nothing written)']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/submit (prep.edit): checks the H2 checklist (no open flags), records signoff H2 through the core decision service, status In review','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack/review (prep.review): approve, or return with comments (required)','Table pack_reviews; events SignOffRecorded:H2, ContextPackSubmitted, ContextPackApproved, ContextPackReturned','Return creates an action for the analyst; approve creates the H1 and H3 actions']::text[],array['Submit button with the H2 checklist shown and blocking items listed','Review view for the lead with Approve and Return with comments; comments per section','Analyst sees returned comments inline and a "Returned" banner']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['What exactly is frozen when the pack is sent for review?','How do you show the lead what changed since the last return?','Which actions must appear on whose Today after each step?']::text[],6224),
('P-04','Sign-offs H1 and H3 with their checklists','Prepare','The lead signs H1 (brief frozen) and H3 (cards signed), each with its checklist from gates.p1.yaml. In Phase 1 only the Immersion lead signs both (roles.p1.yaml signoff_signers). A sign-off is a decision, so it needs step-up and writes the log sentence.','As an Immersion lead I sign the brief and the cards against a checklist, so that the material is locked on purpose and the log shows who signed what.','Prep','dev2',7,false,array['P-03']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (sign-offs)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (signoffs)','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml (signoff_signers)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','backend/src/modules/prep/rules.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/SignOffCard.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/signoffs/:code']::text[],array['Signing with an unticked checklist item is refused','Signing H3 before H2 is refused','Only the Immersion lead can sign (403 for others)','Without step-up the call gets 401 step_up_required']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/signoffs/:code for H1 and H3 with ticked checklist items','Uses the core decision service (signoffs table) so every stage records sign-offs the same way','Refuses unknown codes and H2 or H4 here (they have their own flows)','Events SignOffRecorded:H1 and SignOffRecorded:H3']::text[],array['Sign-off cards in the Prepare tab with checklist, Sign button and signed state with time and role','Blocked state that says what is missing']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place']::text[],array['Where should the sign-off order (H1, H2, H3, then Gate B, then release) live so every module uses the same rule?','What does a stand-in signature look like in the log?','Can a sign-off ever be withdrawn in Phase 1?']::text[],7225),
('P-05','Card ratings and Gate B','Prepare','After H3 the sponsor rates each challenge card for relevance. In Phase 1 the lead records the sponsor''s ratings with an evidence reference. When every card is rated the rule proposes Gate B: passed when at least two thirds are relevant. Not passed creates "Revise the cards".','As an Immersion lead I record how the sponsor rated the cards and confirm Gate B, so that the session only uses challenges the sponsor cares about.','Prep','dev2',7,false,array['P-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (Gate B)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (B)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (rate_cards, confirm_gate_b, revise_cards)','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4 note on Gate B']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','backend/src/modules/prep/rules.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/CardRatings.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/cards/ratings','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/gate-b']::text[],array['Gate B is not proposed until every card is rated','2 of 3 relevant passes; 1 of 3 does not','Evidence reference is required','Not passed creates the revise action and Gate B can be recorded again after revision']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/cards/ratings (records all ratings with the evidence reference) and POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/gate-b (confirm)','Table card_ratings; rule in rules.ts: propose only when rated == total, pass when relevant / total >= 0.667','Decision through the core decision service; events GateProposed:B, GateDecided:B','roles.p1.yaml combine: "Record the sponsor''s card ratings" is one action']::text[],array['Rating table: one row per card, Relevant or Not relevant, evidence reference field','Gate B result with the count, "Revise the cards" state when not passed']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)']::text[],array['Why is the threshold 0.667 and not 2/3 computed as a float, and does it matter for 3, 6 and 9 cards?','What happens to ratings when a card is revised?','Gate B used to sit in Convert: who needs to know it moved?']::text[],7226),
('P-06','Release the material','Prepare','The lead presses Release material. It is allowed only with an approved pack, H1, H2 and H3 signed and Gate B passed. Release locks the pack and cards, moves the client to Immerse, and opens session setup for the lead.','As an Immersion lead I release the material in one press once everything is signed, so that session setup starts from locked, checked content.','Prep','dev2',8,true,array['P-05']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (release)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.6 point 4','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.10 scenario 9']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts','backend/src/modules/prep/index.ts','frontend/src/features/prepare/ReleaseCard.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/material/release']::text[],array['Release with any item missing is refused and lists what is missing','After release nobody can edit the pack or the cards','The client shows in the Immerse column of the stage view','getReleasedMaterial returns the cards and priorities in the shape agreed in the session contract']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/material/release (prep.review, step-up)','One transaction: lock pack and cards, event MaterialReleased, advanceStage to immerse through the clients module','Exposes getReleasedMaterial(clientId) in prep/index.ts for the session module (Developer 3)']::text[],array['Release card with a checklist of what is done and what is missing, and one Release button','After release: locked banner on the pack, stage rail moves to Immerse, link "Set up the session"']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer']::text[],array['What exact data does the session module need from the released material?','What if someone needs to fix a typo after release?','How do you make the release and the stage move one transaction across two modules?']::text[],8227),
('P-07','Prepare tab for each role, with progress','Prepare','The Prepare tab shows a progress strip (pack, H2, review, H1, H3, Gate B, release) and only what each role may do. The Research analyst sees only the Overview and Prepare tabs of a shared card; the consultant and team see Prepare read-only.','As any member I open the Prepare tab and see where preparation stands and what, if anything, is mine to do.','Prep','dev2',7,false,array['P-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/PREPARE.md (tab per role)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.4 (tab table)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.10 scenario 8']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/prepare/PrepareTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/prepare/PrepProgress.tsx','backend/src/modules/prep/service.ts']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/context-pack']::text[],array['A Research analyst sees only Overview and Prepare and gets 404 on Qualify and Convert routes of that card','Every role sees the same progress for the same pack','Buttons a role cannot use are not shown, and the API still refuses them']::text[],array['GET on the context pack returns a progress summary and the caller''s allowed actions (computed from the role table)','Tab visibility comes from contracts/src/roles.ts so frontend and backend agree']::text[],array['Progress strip component (uses the UI kit Stepper or StageRail styles)','Per-role empty states: analyst "Your next step", lead "Waiting for the analyst", team "Read only"']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The frontend hides what a role cannot do, but the backend still refuses it','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Where do you compute "allowed actions" so it cannot drift from the real checks?','What should a member who was added after release see?','How will you test all four roles without four manual sign-ins?']::text[],7228),
('M-01','Session setup: when, where and pods','Immerse','The Immersion lead sets the session date, start time, length and format (on site, online, hybrid) and the pods: name, challenge card and member count. Challenge cards come from the released material. This is the first half of session setup.','As an Immersion lead I set up when the session runs and which pod works on which challenge, so that the day is planned in the app and not in a spreadsheet.','Session','dev3',4,true,array['K-3']::text[],array['prep/index.ts getReleasedMaterial() stub returning seeded cards until P-06 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (session setup)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 1']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/routes.ts','backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','backend/src/modules/session/repo.ts','backend/src/db/schema/session.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/SessionSetupPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/PodsEditor.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/session','PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/session']::text[],array['Setup is refused before the material is released','A pod must have a challenge card from this client''s released cards','Only the lead can change setup; the consultant and team see it read-only','A stale save gets 412']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/session and PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/session (session.setup, If-Match)','Tables sessions and session_pods; one session per client in Phase 1','Reads cards through prep/index.ts getReleasedMaterial()','Event SessionSetupSaved']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/immerse/SessionSetupPage.tsx at /w/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/immerse/setup','Pods editor: add, rename, pick a challenge card, member count; validation messages inline','Locked state with "Release the material first" until Prepare is done']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['What limits make sense (pods per session, members per pod) and where do they live?','What happens to the setup if the material is released again after a fix?','Which time zone is the session time in, and how do you show it?']::text[],4339),
('M-02','Session setup: steps, scoring and feedback','Immerse','The second half of setup: turn steps on or off, order them, set minutes and prompt wording (from step-library.v2.yaml); choose scoring criteria (value and feasibility, risk optional) and votes per pod; up to six feedback questions; and the AI consultant who runs the console.','As an Immersion lead I shape the session agenda and scoring for this customer, so that the day fits their time and goals.','Session','dev3',5,false,array['M-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (steps and scoring)','docs/blueprint/rules/step-library.v2.yaml','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 1, §15.11']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/rules.ts','backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/StepsEditor.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/ScoringPanel.tsx']::text[],array['PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/session']::text[],array['Setup whose steps overrun the session length is refused with the overrun shown','A required step cannot be turned off','Picking a member who is not an AI consultant is refused','Prompt wording passes the names check']::text[],array['Same PUT setup contract, steps part: session_steps from the step library with overrides','Rules: total minutes must fit the session length; required steps cannot be turned off; at most six feedback questions','Consultant must be an active member with the ai_consultant role']::text[],array['Steps list with toggles, minutes, reorder and prompt wording editor; running total against session length','Scoring and votes panel; feedback questions editor; consultant picker']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Which step-library fields can a lead change and which are fixed?','How do you keep the library version with the session?','What is the first thing to cut if this runs late (PHASE1_PLAN §15.11)?']::text[],5330),
('M-03','Preview as participant and publish (H4, join code)','Immerse','"Preview as participant" shows the pod screen with the real setup. "Publish" signs H4 (material released for the session) and issues the join code; the code is created by signing, not before (gates.p1.yaml). Publishing without H1, H3 and an approved pack is refused.','As an Immersion lead I check what participants will see and publish the session, so that the join code exists only when everything is ready.','Session','dev3',5,true,array['M-02']::text[],array['prep/index.ts release status stub until P-06 lands','Step-up stub until A-08 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (publish)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (H4, on_signed)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 1']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','backend/src/modules/session/codes.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/PublishDialog.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/JoinCodeCard.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/publish','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/code/rotate','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/code/revoke']::text[],array['Publish without H1, H3 and an approved context pack is refused (PHASE1_PLAN §15.10 scenario 9)','The code appears only after H4 is signed','Rotate makes the old code fail at once','The code is never in logs or events']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/publish (session.setup, step-up): checks release state, signs H4 through the core decision service, creates session_codes row','Join code: 8 characters from an unambiguous alphabet, stored hashed, expires at session end','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/code/rotate and POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/code/revoke','Events SignOffRecorded:H4, SessionPublished, SessionCodeIssued (code never in the event)']::text[],array['Preview opens the participant pod screen in a frame with a "Preview" banner and no writes','Publish dialog with the checklist; after publish the code is shown large with Copy, Rotate and Revoke']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer']::text[],array['How long should a join code be so it is easy to type but hard to guess, given the rate limit?','How do you make preview impossible to write data from?','What happens to joined pods when the code is rotated?']::text[],5331),
('M-04','Join a session: code, pod, notice','Immerse','A participant opens /join, types the session code, picks their pod, reads the notice and lands on Step 0. No account and no QR code. The pod works on one shared screen, so the device gets a pod device token, not a person''s identity.','As a participant I join my pod with a short code in under a minute, so that the session starts on time.','Session','dev3',6,true,array['M-03']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (join)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 2']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/participant-routes.ts','backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/participant/JoinPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/participant/PodPicker.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/s/join','POST /api/s/pod','GET /api/s/state']::text[],array['A wrong code gives the same answer as an expired one','A pod device token cannot read another pod''s entries','Joining after revoke is refused','The join flow works on a tablet and passes axe']::text[],array['Public routes under /api/s: POST /api/s/join (code), POST /api/s/pod (pick pod), GET /api/s/state','pod_devices table: random token hashed, cookie scoped to /api/s, expires at session end','Rate limit on join per address (10 a minute) and a lockout per code after many failures','Participant routes never reach staff data; only this session and this pod']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/participant/JoinPage.tsx at /join: code field, pod picker, notice, then the pod screen','Errors: wrong code, session not started, session ended, pod full','Large text and buttons for a shared screen']::text[],array['Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['What does the notice say about data, and where does its text come from?','How do you stop someone at home joining with a code they saw on a slide?','What happens when the shared screen reloads mid-step?']::text[],6332),
('M-05','Pod screen: work the steps and ask for help','Immerse','The pod screen shows the current step, its prompt and a timer, and a shared entry area where the pod writes its ideas. A "We are stuck" button raises a flag on the consultant console. Steps move on when the consultant or the timer says so.','As a pod of participants we work through each step on one screen and ask for help when stuck, so that we finish with ideas worth scoring.','Session','dev3',6,false,array['M-04']::text[],array['The core stream (GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/stream) from Developer 1; poll every 3 seconds behind the same hook until C-01 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (pod screen)','docs/blueprint/rules/step-library.v2.yaml','docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (pod screen)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/participant/PodScreen.tsx','frontend/src/features/participant/StepTimer.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/s/steps/:stepId','POST /api/s/help']::text[],array['Entries survive a page reload','A stuck flag appears on the console within 2 seconds','Names in entries are flagged before save','A pod cannot write to a step that is not current']::text[],array['POST /api/s/steps/:stepId (save pod entries), POST /api/s/help (raise stuck flag)','Tables step_entries and help_requests; entries pass the names check','Live updates to the pod and the console through the core stream (server-sent events)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/participant/PodScreen.tsx: step header, prompt, timer, entry list, add and edit entry, We are stuck button','Reconnect banner when the stream drops; entries kept on screen and resent']::text[],array['Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['Who moves the pod to the next step, and what if the timer and the consultant disagree?','How do you avoid lost entries if two people type on the shared screen?','What does the pod see while waiting for help?']::text[],6333),
('M-06','Consultant console: watch pods and help','Immerse','The AI consultant sees every pod with its step and time left, and stuck flags. "Help this pod" sends a hint to that pod''s screen and clears the flag. The console also rotates or revokes the code and moves steps on.','As an AI consultant I see which pod is stuck and send help at once, so that no pod loses time in the session.','Session','dev3',7,true,array['M-05']::text[],array['Polling stand-in for the core stream until C-01 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (console)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 3','docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (console)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/ConsolePage.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/PodGrid.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/HintDialog.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/console','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/pods/:podId/hint']::text[],array['A hint reaches the pod screen within 2 seconds and clears the flag','Only the AI consultant and the lead can use the console (403 for team, 404 for analyst)','The console works on a laptop at 1280 pixels and a tablet']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/console (session.run), POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/pods/:podId/hint','Hint text passes the names check; event HintSent; flag cleared in the same transaction','Step control for the session (next step, extend time) with its event']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/immerse/ConsolePage.tsx at /w/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/console','Pod grid: step, time left, stuck badge sorted to the top, Help this pod dialog with quick hints from the step library','Live updates; a clear offline banner']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What does the consultant need to see in under one second when a pod is stuck?','How will you test the console and the pod screen together?','What happens if the consultant''s laptop disconnects?']::text[],7334),
('M-07','Decision block: scores, votes and feedback','Immerse','The consultant opens the decision block. Each pod agrees one score per idea on the chosen criteria and casts its votes, but not all on its own idea. Then each member gives feedback in turn on the shared screen. The consultant closes the block.','As a pod we score and vote fairly on all ideas and give feedback, so that the decision is based on the room and not on the loudest voice.','Session','dev3',7,false,array['M-06']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (decision block)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 4']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/rules.ts','backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/participant/DecisionBlock.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/decision-block','POST /api/s/scores','POST /api/s/votes','POST /api/s/feedback']::text[],array['All votes on the pod''s own idea are refused','Scores outside the range are refused','Writes after close are refused','Feedback answers pass the names check']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/decision-block (open or close)','Participant routes POST /api/s/scores, POST /api/s/votes, POST /api/s/feedback','Rules in rules.ts: votes per pod from setup, not all on the pod''s own idea, scores within the criteria range','Tables idea_scores, votes, feedback_entries; writes refused when the block is closed']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/participant/DecisionBlock.tsx: score each idea, cast votes with a counter, then feedback questions in turn','Console shows which pods have finished']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['What exactly does "not all on its own idea" mean with 3 votes? Write the table test first','What if a pod never finishes voting before close?','How do you show anonymous feedback without showing who wrote it?']::text[],7335),
('M-08','Results: chart, votes and feedback summary','Immerse','After the block, the consultant sees a value and feasibility chart of the ideas, the vote counts and a feedback summary. This is the screen used in the room to agree the one or two ideas that go forward.','As an AI consultant I show the room a clear picture of the scores and votes, so that the sponsor can choose with everyone watching.','Session','dev3',8,false,array['M-07']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (results)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.7 point 5']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/ResultsPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/IdeaChart.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/results']::text[],array['Totals match the stored scores and votes','The chart has a table alternative for screen readers','The Immersion team sees results read-only; the analyst gets 404']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/results (session.run and session.view): aggregates scores and votes per idea, feedback counts and text']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/immerse/ResultsPage.tsx: scatter chart (value against feasibility) with labels, votes table, feedback summary','Chart readable on a projector and accessible as a table']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['How do you label overlapping ideas on the chart?','Which numbers will people argue about, and can they trace each one back?','What should the screen show before the block is closed?']::text[],8336),
('M-09','Decision memo and Gate C','Immerse','The consultant prepares the decision memo from the results: one or two ideas, each with title, one-line summary, business owner role and data owner role, V1 labelled Estimate, and the next step with a date. Then records the sponsor''s choice (Gate C: go, customer-led, no-go). The client moves to Convert.','As an AI consultant I record the sponsor''s decision in the room with a complete memo, so that the follow-up can start the same day.','Session','dev3',8,true,array['M-08']::text[],array['Step-up stub until A-08 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (Gate C)','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (C)','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml (overrides)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (sign_memo)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/service.ts','backend/src/modules/session/index.ts (getDecisionMemo for convert)','frontend/src/features/immerse/MemoForm.tsx','frontend/src/features/immerse/GateCDialog.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/memo','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/gate-c']::text[],array['A memo without owner roles or a next step date is refused','Gate C go moves the client to Convert and the follow-up action appears for the Immersion team','Without step-up the call is refused','Owner fields refuse personal names']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/memo (draft memo, then prepared), POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/gate-c (step-up, evidence reference)','Table decision_memos; Gate C through the core decision service; advanceStage to convert','Events DecisionMemoPrepared, GateDecided:C; roles.p1.yaml: gate_c and sign_memo by the AI consultant']::text[],array['Memo form prefilled from the top ideas; role pickers (role titles only); V1 with unit and value type','Gate C dialog: outcome, evidence reference, confirm with step-up']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Other modules are used only through their index.ts']::text[],array['What does Developer 4 need from the memo to draft the follow-up note?','What does "V1 recorded: yes" mean when customer numbers are not stored?','How does a no-go still leave the door open (check-in)?']::text[],8337),
('M-10','Offline export of the session','Immerse','If the network fails in the room, the session must still run. The lead or consultant downloads a printable pack (pods, steps, prompts, scoring sheets) and later a results export. The export contains no participant identities.','As an AI consultant I have a printed fallback for the session, so that a bad connection does not stop the day.','Session','dev3',8,false,array['M-03']::text[],array['In-process file builder until F-01 (worker) and F-03 (storage) land']::text[],array['docs/stages/IMMERSE.md (offline)','docs/blueprint/SPEC.md (offline fallback)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/session/export.ts','frontend/src/features/immerse/ExportButtons.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/export']::text[],array['The printable pack matches the published setup','The results export totals match the results screen','No pod device tokens or names in any export']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sessions/:sessionId/export (pdf or csv, session.run)','Generated by the worker (Developer 4) with a stub that builds the file in process until the worker lands','Event SessionExported']::text[],array['Export buttons on the setup and results pages; progress and download states']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What is the smallest export that still lets the session run on paper?','How do paper results get back into the app?','Where is the file stored and for how long?']::text[],8338),
('V-01','Customer contacts','Convert','The Immersion team adds customer contacts, one per customer role, work email only, with the purpose "deal messages". Contacts are the only place a customer email lives, so they sit in the pii schema and approved messages go only to them.','As an Immersion team member I keep the customer contacts for this client in one place, so that approved messages reach the right roles.','Convert','dev4',4,false,array['K-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (contacts)','docs/blueprint/acceptance/phase1.feature (Customer contacts and sending)','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml (contacts)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/convert/routes.ts','backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts','backend/src/modules/convert/repo.ts','backend/src/db/schema/convert.ts','frontend/src/features/convert/ConvertTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/convert/ContactsSection.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts','DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts/:contactId']::text[],array['A free-mail address domain is refused with a clear reason (rule list in rules.ts)','The email never appears in events, logs or the live log','A Research analyst gets 404; the AI consultant sees role titles only','A second contact for the same role is refused']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts, POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts, DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/contacts/:contactId (convert.work)','Table pii.contacts: role title, work email, purpose; never copied into events or drafts','Events ContactAdded, ContactRemoved (role title only)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/convert/ContactsSection.tsx in the Convert tab: list, add dialog (role title, work email), remove with confirm','Help text: "One contact per customer role. Work email only. No personal names."']::text[],array['Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400']::text[],array['How do you keep the email out of every log line, including validation errors?','Who may see the email itself, and who only the role title?','What happens to contacts when a client is closed?']::text[],4449),
('V-02','Agent drafting service (drafts only)','Convert','The agent module turns structured input (the decision memo, the client facts) into a draft for a person to edit and approve. In Phase 1 drafts come from versioned templates, not a language model. Agents never send and never decide.','As an Immersion team member I start from a good draft, so that I spend my time checking it and not typing it.','Convert','dev4',5,true,array['K-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (agent drafts)','docs/blueprint/SPEC.md (agents draft, people decide)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/agent/index.ts','backend/src/modules/agent/templates/*','backend/src/modules/agent/agent.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['draft() has no way to send mail (no mail import in the agent module, checked by the boundary lint)','The same input gives the same draft','agent_runs never stores draft content or contact emails','Each template has a unit test with invented data']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/agent/index.ts: draft(kind, input) returns { subject, body, sources }','Templates per kind (followup_note, expectation_statement) with a version; agent_runs table records kind, template version, input ids (no content)','Output passes the names check; a draft that fails is marked for review, not blocked silently']::text[],array['None (V-03 shows drafts)']::text[],array['Agents only draft; a person approves and sends; agents never decide','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place']::text[],array['Which facts may a draft quote, and how does it cite where each came from?','How would you swap templates for a model later without changing callers?','What makes a draft "needs review" rather than ready?']::text[],5440),
('V-03','Follow-up note: draft, approve and send','Convert','After Gate C the Immersion team gets "Approve and send the follow-up note", due within 2 working days. The agent drafts it from the memo; a team member edits, approves and presses Send to customer, picking the contact roles. Sending goes through the worker and mail adapter.','As an Immersion team member I send an approved follow-up within two days of the session, so that the customer''s interest does not fade.','Convert','dev4',6,true,array['V-01','V-02']::text[],array['session/index.ts getDecisionMemo() stub with a seeded memo until M-09 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (follow-up)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (approve_followup)','docs/blueprint/acceptance/phase1.feature (sending)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts','frontend/src/features/convert/FollowupEditor.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/followup/draft','PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId/approve','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId/send']::text[],array['Send without approval is refused','Send to an address that is not a contact of this client is impossible (ids only, not emails, in the request)','The mail arrives in Mailpit with the approved text','Editing after approval sets it back to Draft']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/followup/draft, PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId, POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId/approve, POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/drafts/:draftId/send','Table drafts with status Draft, Approved, Sent; send only from Approved, only to contacts of this client','Send enqueues a send-email job; event DraftSent with contact role titles only']::text[],array['Draft editor with source notes, Approve and Send to customer with a contact role picker','Sent state with time and roles; resend refused']::text[],array['Agents only draft; a person approves and sends; agents never decide','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What if the mail provider fails after the draft is marked Sent?','Who approves if the author is the only team member?','How will the decision memo reach you before Developer 3 finishes Gate C?']::text[],6441),
('V-04','Decision meeting record','Convert','Within 10 working days of the session the sponsor holds a decision meeting. The team records the outcome: Gate C confirmed or changed, and whether the sprint order was signed, with an evidence reference.','As an Immersion team member I record what the sponsor decided in the meeting, so that the sprint can start or the reason is on file.','Convert','dev4',7,false,array['V-03']::text[],array['Step-up stub until A-08 lands','Working-day helper stub until C-02 lands']::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (decision meeting)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (hold_decision_meeting)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts','frontend/src/features/convert/DecisionMeetingForm.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/decision-meeting']::text[],array['Missing evidence reference is refused','Sprint order signed creates the "Record sprint day 1" action','The record cannot be changed after sprint day 1 is recorded']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/decision-meeting (convert.work, step-up)','Table decision_meetings: date, outcome, sprintOrderSigned, evidence reference','Event DecisionMeetingRecorded; when sprintOrderSigned the start_sprint action appears']::text[],array['Meeting form in the Convert tab; due chip "within 10 working days of the session"; overdue badge']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['What if the sponsor changes the Gate C outcome in the meeting?','Which working-day function do you use, and who owns it?','What does the log sentence say?']::text[],7442),
('V-05','Readiness items','Convert','Contract, data terms and security reviews take longer than any other step, so they start after H1. The team keeps a readiness checklist per client: item, owner role, due date, state, and a note. Items block sprint day 1 until done or waived with a reason.','As an Immersion team member I track contract, data and security readiness, so that the sprint is not blocked on paperwork.','Convert','dev4',7,false,array['V-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (readiness)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (start_readiness)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts','backend/src/modules/convert/rules.ts','frontend/src/features/convert/ReadinessList.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/readiness','PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/readiness']::text[],array['A waived item needs a reason','Owner must be a role title','Sprint day 1 is refused while an item is open']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/readiness and PUT /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/readiness (convert.work, If-Match)','Table readiness_items; default items from a list in rules.ts','Events ReadinessItemChanged']::text[],array['Readiness checklist with owner role, due chip and state; waive with reason']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['Which readiness items exist by default, and who decided?','What is "done" for a security review?','How do readiness due dates relate to the session date?']::text[],7443),
('V-06','Sprint day 1 and check-ins','Convert','The team records sprint day 1 (the fast path aims for within 4 weeks of Gate C). Check-ins at 2 and 4 weeks keep the deal warm; the 4-week check-in asks for the outcome testimonial with consent. After sprint day 1 the client shows Prove as Phase 2.','As an Immersion team member I record the sprint start and hold the check-ins, so that every deal ends with a dated next step.','Convert','dev4',8,false,array['V-04','V-05']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (sprint day 1, check-ins)','docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (start_sprint, checkin_2w, checkin_4w)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts','frontend/src/features/convert/SprintStartCard.tsx','frontend/src/features/convert/CheckinList.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/sprint-start','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/checkins']::text[],array['Sprint day 1 needs a signed sprint order from the decision meeting','Check-in actions appear at 2 and 4 weeks after Gate C','Testimonial is stored only with consent']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/sprint-start and POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/checkins','Tables sprint_starts and checkins; events SprintStarted, CheckinRecorded','Sprint start refused while readiness items are open']::text[],array['Sprint start card with date and evidence reference; check-in list with due chips; testimonial consent checkbox']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What does Prove locked look like in the stage rail after sprint day 1?','Where is consent stored, and who can see it?','What if sprint day 1 is later than 4 weeks?']::text[],8444),
('V-07','Convert tab for each role, and a reasoned no-go','Convert','The Convert tab brings contacts, follow-up, meeting, readiness, sprint and check-ins together with a progress strip. The lead and team can work; the consultant sees it read-only. A client can be closed as a reasoned no-go with a check-in date, which keeps the door open.','As an Immersion team member I see everything left to convert this client on one tab, and close it properly if the answer is no.','Convert','dev4',8,false,array['V-06']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/CONVERT.md (Convert tab)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.4 (tab table), §15.8']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/convert/ConvertTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/convert/CloseNoGoDialog.tsx','backend/src/modules/convert/service.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['The consultant sees Convert read-only; the analyst gets 404','No-go without a reason is refused','A closed client shows in the stage view as closed with its check-in date']::text[],array['Close as no-go: reason and check-in date required, event DealClosed, checkin_closed action']::text[],array['Progress strip and sections; per-role empty states; Close as no-go dialog']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','The frontend hides what a role cannot do, but the backend still refuses it','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Which sections are empty for a customer-led next step?','How does a closed client look in the customer view and the stage view?','What should Today show the team for this client?']::text[],8445),
('C-01','Live log and live updates','Shared','Every client card has a live log beside it: one plain sentence per event, newest first. Open screens update without a reload through server-sent events fed by Postgres LISTEN and NOTIFY. Other stages use the same stream for their own screens.','As any member I see what just happened on a client as it happens, so that I never work on stale information.','Core','dev1',3,true,array['K-1']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/stages/QUALIFY.md (live log)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §4.4 (log sentences)','docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (live log)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/clients/stream.ts','backend/src/modules/clients/rules.ts (sentences)','frontend/src/features/clients/LiveLog.tsx','frontend/src/lib/useLiveStream.ts']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/events','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/stream']::text[],array['A member who cannot see a card never receives its events on the stream','Every event type has a sentence and a test','The stream reconnects after a dropped connection without duplicates','Removing a member closes their open streams']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId/events (paged, visibility checked)','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/stream: server-sent events, one connection per tab, only events the caller may see','Sentence builder in rules.ts: one sentence per event type, role titles only, stand-in wording ("recorded for the sponsor")','NOTIFY on recordEvent; heartbeat every 25 seconds; limits on open connections per user']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/clients/LiveLog.tsx beside the card; useLiveStream() hook in frontend/src/lib with reconnect and back-off','Offline banner, "New events" pill when scrolled away']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['How do you filter stream events by visibility without a query per event?','What is your plan when 40 people have the app open?','Which sentence wording rules from the prototype must every stage follow?']::text[],3516),
('C-02','Actions engine with working-day due dates','Shared','Events create actions by the rules in workflow.p1.yaml: owner role (resolved through the roles.p1.yaml stand-ins), title, why, due date in working days from an anchor (event, session, Gate C). Combined actions from roles.p1.yaml become one action. Every stage gets its next steps from here.','As any member I get the right next action at the right time with a due date, so that nothing waits for someone to remember it.','Core','dev1',4,true,array['C-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §4.2, §5']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/clients/actions.ts','backend/src/modules/clients/rules.ts (working days, resolveActor)','backend/src/modules/clients/actions.test.ts']::text[],array['POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/actions/:actionId/complete']::text[],array['A table-driven test covers every action in workflow.p1.yaml that Phase 1 creates','Due dates skip weekends and listed holidays','Combined actions (record_exception then approve_exception) appear as one action','Completing an action someone else owns is refused']::text[],array['Engine in clients/service.ts subscribed to recordEvent: matches on/when, resolves owner with resolveActor(), stores ownerRole and onBehalfOfRole','Working-day maths in rules.ts (weekends and a holiday list), offset_wd, min_lead_wd','Table actions; phase2_only actions never created; events ActionCreated, ActionCompleted','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/actions/:actionId/complete']::text[],array['None beyond the Today page (C-03)']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','Other modules are used only through their index.ts']::text[],array['How do you test this engine without running the whole app?','What happens when the anchor (the session date) changes after the action was created?','Which actions does each stage owner expect, and have they confirmed it?']::text[],4517),
('C-03','Today: my actions across clients','Shared','Today is the landing page after sign-in: the actions for my role across the clients I can see, grouped by due (overdue, today, this week, later), each with the client label, why, and a button that opens the right tab.','As any member I open the app and see exactly what is mine to do today, so that I do not hunt through client cards.','Core','dev1',5,false,array['C-02']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (Today)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §5']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx','backend/src/modules/clients/routes.ts']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/actions']::text[],array['Actions on cards the member cannot see never appear','Overdue actions are first and marked','Each action opens the right tab of the right client']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/actions?mine=true (only visible clients, only my role or my user)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx at /w/:workspaceId/today with groups, due chips and overdue badges','Empty state "Nothing due. Well done." and a link to Clients']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Which actions belong to a role and which to a person?','How should a stand-in action read differently?','What does Today look like for a Research analyst with no clients yet?']::text[],5518),
('C-04','Decisions, sign-offs and stage moves','Shared','One service records every gate decision and sign-off (gate_decisions, signoffs) with step-up, evidence reference and the log sentence, and one function moves a client to the next stage. Prepare, Immerse and Convert call these through clients/index.ts so every stage records decisions the same way.','As a stage owner I record a gate or sign-off with one call, so that the rules, the log and the stage rail stay the same across stages.','Core','dev1',3,true,array['K-1']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml','docs/blueprint/rules/roles.p1.yaml (evidence_ref_required)','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §8, §10']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/clients/decisions.ts','backend/src/modules/clients/index.ts','backend/src/modules/clients/rules.ts (stage order)']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Moving a client backwards or skipping a stage is refused','A decision listed in evidence_ref_required without a reference is refused','Each call writes its event in the caller''s transaction','A stub version of every function is merged in week 3 so other stages can call it']::text[],array['clients/index.ts: recordDecision(tx, {gate, outcome, evidenceRef, actingRole, onBehalfOfRole}), recordSignOff(tx, {code, checklist}), advanceStage(tx, clientId, to)','Stage order and allowed moves in rules.ts; Prove, Pilot and Scale refused in Phase 1','Events GateDecided:<gate>:<outcome>, SignOffRecorded:<code>, StageChanged','evidence_ref_required list from roles.p1.yaml enforced here']::text[],array['Stage rail updates from StageChanged on the live stream']::text[],array['The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Other modules are used only through their index.ts','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes']::text[],array['What is the exact function signature each stage needs? Ask the other three before writing it','How do you keep the transaction owned by the caller?','Where is the "two deciders must agree" rule for later phases?']::text[],3519),
('C-05','Reminders and escalations','Shared','A daily job sends reminders for actions due tomorrow and escalates overdue actions to the Immersion lead after one working day (workflow.p1.yaml defaults). Customer reminders are drafted for the Immersion team, never sent automatically.','As an Immersion lead I hear about overdue work without checking every card, so that deadlines before the session are kept.','Core','dev1',7,false,array['C-02']::text[],array['Worker and mail adapter stubs (run in process, log to console) until F-01 and F-02 land']::text[],array['docs/blueprint/rules/workflow.p1.yaml (defaults, reminder)']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/clients/reminders.ts','backend/src/modules/clients/reminders.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Running the job twice on the same day sends nothing new','Actions with escalation_role none are never escalated','Customer-facing reminders become drafts, not mails']::text[],array['Job reminders.daily registered with the worker; idempotent per action and day','Escalation rules per action (escalation_role, escalation_after_wd, none)','Mail through the mail adapter; events ReminderSent, ActionEscalated']::text[],array['Escalated badge on Today and on the card']::text[],array['Agents only draft; a person approves and sends; agents never decide','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place']::text[],array['What time zone is "tomorrow" in?','How do you test a daily job without waiting a day?','What if the mail adapter is down?']::text[],7510),
('C-06','Client card overview: next action and key facts','Shared','The Overview tab and each card in the customer view show the next action and its due chip, an overdue badge, key facts (industry, function, format, planned session date) and the stage rail with done, current and later stages.','As any member I understand a client in five seconds from its card, so that I know where it stands and what is next.','Core','dev1',6,false,array['C-03']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.4','docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (client cards)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/clients/OverviewTab.tsx','frontend/src/features/clients/ClientCard.tsx','backend/src/modules/clients/repo.ts']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients','GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/clients/:clientId']::text[],array['The list of 50 clients loads in one query for next actions','Overdue badge matches Today','The card reads well on a phone']::text[],array['Client list and detail return nextAction and overdue (one query, no N+1)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/clients/OverviewTab.tsx and the card in the customer view updated with next action and badges','Stage view columns show overdue counts']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Database access only in repo.ts, every query scoped by workspaceId','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['How do you get next action for every card without a query per card?','What does a closed or no-go client card look like?','Which facts are safe to show to every role?']::text[],6511),
('A-01','Verify email after register','Shared','Register already creates an unverified account. Add the verification email: a one-time link valid for 24 hours, a resend option, and sign-in refused until verified. The development auto-verify setting must stay impossible in production.','As a new user I confirm my work email before I can sign in, so that nobody can register with someone else''s address.','Access','dev2',2,true,array['S-2']::text[],array['Mail adapter console stub until F-02 lands; read the link from the server log in development only']::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.1 point 1','GUARDRAILS.md (auth)','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/service.ts','backend/src/modules/access/routes.ts','backend/src/db/schema/access.ts','frontend/src/features/auth/VerifyPage.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/register','POST /api/auth/verify-email']::text[],array['Sign-in is refused until the email is verified','A token works once and expires after 24 hours','Register with an existing email gives the same answer and sends no new account','Config refuses to start in production with auto-verify on']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/verify-email with the token; email_tokens table (hash only, purpose, expiry, used_at)','Register always answers "Check your email", whether or not the address exists','Mail sent through the mail adapter (console stub until F-02)','Event-free (account events are not deal events); audit line in the auth log']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/auth/VerifyPage.tsx at /verify?token=…, "Check your email" page with resend after 60 seconds','Clear expired and used link states']::text[],array['Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['How do you stop register being used to find out who has an account?','Where can the token leak (logs, referrer) and how do you stop it?','What should happen if the user clicks the link while signed in as someone else?']::text[],2522),
('A-02','Forgot and reset password','Shared','"Forgot password" sends a one-time link valid for 30 minutes. Reset sets a new password, ends every other session of that user and clears any lockout. The answer is the same whether or not the email exists.','As a user who forgot my password I get back in safely, and anyone using my old password is signed out.','Access','dev2',3,false,array['A-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.1 point 2']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/service.ts','frontend/src/features/auth/ForgotPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/auth/ResetPage.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/password/forgot','POST /api/auth/password/reset']::text[],array['The answer to forgot is the same for known and unknown emails','A reset token works once and expires after 30 minutes','After reset, old sessions are signed out']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/password/forgot and POST /api/auth/password/reset; tokens in email_tokens with purpose reset','Reset ends all auth_sessions of the user and rotates the current one']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/auth/ForgotPage.tsx and ResetPage.tsx with password rules shown as you type']::text[],array['Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What if two reset emails are requested: does the first link still work?','Should reset sign the user in, or send them to sign in?','How do you rate limit forgot per email as well as per address?']::text[],3523),
('A-03','Password strength and breached-password check','Shared','Passwords must be 12 characters or more and must not be on a breached or common password list. The list is shipped with the app (no external call with the password), and the same check runs on register, reset and the intake form password.','As a user I am stopped from choosing a password attackers already know, so that my account stays mine.','Access','dev2',3,false,array['A-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.1 point 1','GUARDRAILS.md (passwords)']::text[],array['backend/src/core/password.ts','backend/src/core/common-passwords.txt','backend/src/core/password.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['"password1234" and "Welcome2026!" are refused','A long random passphrase passes','No password is sent to any external service']::text[],array['core/password.ts: checkPasswordStrength(pw) using a bundled list of common passwords (loaded once, stored as a Set of hashes)','Used by register, reset and the intake form password (Developer 1 calls it)']::text[],array['Password field from the UI kit shows length and "This password is too common" before submit']::text[],array['Pure rules in rules.ts with table-driven tests; rules/*.yaml never edited in place','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','The frontend hides what a role cannot do, but the backend still refuses it']::text[],array['Where does the list come from, how big is it, and what is its licence?','Why not call an online breached-password service in Phase 1?','How do you tell the user why a password was refused without helping attackers?']::text[],3524),
('A-04','Invite a member','Shared','Only the Immersion lead invites people: email plus role. The invite link is valid for 7 days and stored as a keyed hash. An email outside the workspace''s allowed domains asks the lead to confirm twice. The lead can list and revoke pending invites.','As an Immersion lead I invite my team with the right role, so that only people I chose can enter our workspace.','Access','dev2',3,true,array['S-2']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.3']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/invites.ts','backend/src/modules/access/routes.ts','frontend/src/features/team/InviteDialog.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites','POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites','DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites/:inviteId']::text[],array['Non-leads get 403 and nothing is written','An invite to an outside domain without the second confirm is refused','A revoked invite link no longer opens','The invite token is never shown again after creation']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites, POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites, DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/invites/:inviteId (team.manage)','invites table: email, role, token hash (HMAC with a server key), expires_at, created_by, accepted_at, revoked_at','Only an existing lead can invite another lead','Mail through the mail adapter']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/team/InviteDialog.tsx: email, role, double confirm for outside domains; pending invites list with Revoke']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs']::text[],array['Why a keyed hash (HMAC) and not a plain hash for invite tokens?','What happens if the same email is invited twice?','Where are the allowed domains set, and who can change them?']::text[],3525),
('A-05','Accept an invite','Shared','The invited person opens the link, signs in or registers with that same email, and accepts. A membership is created with the invited role. A different signed-in email does not open the invite. "Waiting for an invite" lists pending invites for that email.','As an invited person I join the workspace in two clicks, so that I can start on the clients the lead shares with me.','Access','dev2',4,false,array['A-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.3','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.10 scenarios 1 and 2']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/invites.ts','frontend/src/features/onboarding/AcceptInvitePage.tsx','frontend/src/features/onboarding/WaitingPage.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/invites/:token','POST /api/invites/:token/accept']::text[],array['An invite opened with a different email is refused and writes nothing (§15.10 scenario 2)','An expired invite shows a clear message and a way to ask for a new one','Accepting twice creates one membership']::text[],array['GET /api/invites/:token (preview: workspace name and role only), POST /api/invites/:token/accept','Accept checks the signed-in email matches, the invite is open, and creates the membership in one transaction']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/onboarding/AcceptInvitePage.tsx at /invite/:token; Waiting page shows pending invites with Accept']::text[],array['Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Create routes honour Idempotency-Key: the same key returns the first answer','Every screen has loading, empty and error states']::text[],array['What should the preview show to someone who is not signed in?','What if the person already has a membership in this workspace?','How does the requested role from onboarding relate to the invited role?']::text[],4526),
('A-06','Team page: roles, suspend, remove','Shared','The Team page lists members with email, role and status. The lead can change a role, suspend or remove a member, with step-up. The last lead cannot be removed or demoted. Suspending or removing ends that member''s sessions in the workspace.','As an Immersion lead I manage who is in my workspace and what they can do, so that access matches the real team.','Access','dev2',4,false,array['A-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.3']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/members.ts','frontend/src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/members','PATCH /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/members/:memberId']::text[],array['Removing the last lead is refused','A suspended member gets 404 on every workspace route at once','Only leads see the Team page; others get 404']::text[],array['GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/members, PATCH /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/members/:memberId (role, status)','Rule: at least one active lead always; cannot change your own role','Membership changes are workspace events (MemberRoleChanged, MemberSuspended, MemberRemoved)']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx at /w/:workspaceId/team with role select, Suspend, Remove and confirms']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','The change and its event commit in one transaction (recordEvent)','Edits send If-Match with the version; a stale version gets 412 and writes nothing','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['What happens to actions owned by a removed member?','How do you end their live streams and sessions straight away?','Should a suspended member see anything at all?']::text[],4527),
('A-07','Two-step check with an authenticator app','Shared','Users can turn on an authenticator app (TOTP) with recovery codes. An Immersion lead must turn it on before recording their first decision. Sign-in then asks for the six-digit code.','As an Immersion lead I protect my account with a second step, so that a stolen password cannot record decisions.','Access','dev2',5,false,array['A-02']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.1 point 3']::text[],array['backend/src/modules/access/mfa.ts','frontend/src/features/auth/MfaEnrolPage.tsx','frontend/src/features/auth/MfaCodePage.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/mfa/enrol','POST /api/auth/mfa/verify']::text[],array['A lead without MFA is asked to enrol before any decision route','A code works once in its time window','A recovery code works once','The secret is never returned after enrolment']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/mfa/enrol (secret encrypted at rest, QR data), POST /api/auth/mfa/verify','Ten single-use recovery codes, hashed','Sign-in with MFA on: password then code, with its own lockout']::text[],array['frontend/src/features/auth/MfaEnrolPage.tsx with QR, manual key and code check; recovery codes shown once with Download']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['Where is the encryption key for TOTP secrets, and how is it rotated?','What does support do when a lead loses their phone and codes?','How much clock drift do you allow?']::text[],5528),
('A-08','Step-up check before decisions','Shared','Gate decisions and sign-offs need a fresh check: password or authenticator code within the last 5 minutes. A route marks itself step-up in its contract; the core guard answers 401 step_up_required, and the frontend shows a small dialog and retries. Merge the stub in week 2 so every stage can mark routes early.','As an Immersion lead I confirm it is really me before a decision, so that an unattended laptop cannot record one.','Access','dev2',5,true,array['A-07']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.1 point 3','docs/blueprint/rules/gates.p1.yaml (step_up)']::text[],array['backend/src/core/auth.ts (requireStepUp)','backend/src/modules/access/routes.ts','frontend/src/lib/api.ts','frontend/src/features/auth/StepUpDialog.tsx']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/step-up']::text[],array['A decision route without fresh step-up returns 401 step_up_required and writes nothing','After step-up the retried call succeeds','Step-up expires after 5 minutes']::text[],array['POST /api/auth/step-up; auth_sessions.stepped_up_at','core/auth.ts requireStepUp guard driven by the contract flag; stub that passes in development merged first','Every route using step-up gets a test for the 401 case']::text[],array['frontend/src/lib/api.ts handles step_up_required: opens StepUpDialog, retries once']::text[],array['Decisions need a fresh sign-in check (step-up) from the last 5 minutes','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Public routes are rate limited and give the same answer whether or not the thing exists']::text[],array['Which routes in all four stages are decisions? List them with the other owners','How do you retry a write safely after step-up (idempotency)?','What does step-up mean for a user without MFA?']::text[],5529),
('A-09','Access test: every endpoint for every role','Shared','One automated test walks every contract in contracts/src and calls it as each role (lead, team, analyst, consultant), as a member of another workspace and signed out. It checks the answer against the permission table: 401, 403, 404 or allowed, and that a refused write changed nothing.','As the team we know every endpoint enforces the role table, so that a missed check is caught by CI and not by a customer.','Access','dev2',6,true,array['A-06']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5','contracts/src/roles.ts','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.4 (tab table)']::text[],array['backend/test/access-matrix.test.ts','backend/test/fixtures-for-contracts.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Every contract appears in the matrix, including stubs (501 counts only for allowed roles)','A route registered without a permission fails the test','The test runs in under 60 seconds']::text[],array['backend/test/access-matrix.test.ts generated from the contracts list and contracts/src/roles.ts','Row counts before and after each refused write must match','Runs in pnpm verify and in CI']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Routes only through defineRoute with a contract and a permission']::text[],array['How do you build valid input for every endpoint automatically (fixtures)?','Why is 404 the right answer for another workspace?','How will other developers add their new endpoints to the matrix without thinking about it?']::text[],6520),
('U-01','Design tokens, themes and layout shell','Shared','Finish the tokens from the prototype (colours, type, spacing, radius) for light and dark, and polish the shell: top bar, left nav that becomes bottom tabs on phones, main column and live log column. Everyone builds on this, so it lands first.','As any user I get one calm, consistent look on every screen and every device, so that the app feels like one product.','UI kit','dev3',2,true,array['S-3']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (styles and layout)','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3']::text[],array['frontend/src/styles/tokens.css','frontend/src/styles/base.css','frontend/src/app/Layout.tsx','frontend/src/app/DevKitPage.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Colours meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes (checked by a script)','The shell works from 360 to 1440 pixels with no horizontal scroll','No raw colour values outside tokens.css (lint rule)']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['frontend/src/styles/tokens.css and base.css complete; dark theme with prefers-color-scheme and a manual switch','frontend/src/app/Layout.tsx: responsive shell matching prototype/index.html','A /dev/kit page (development only) that shows every token and component']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Which prototype values are tokens and which are one-offs?','How will the other three know which token to use?','What breaks first on a 360-pixel phone?']::text[],2531),
('U-02','Form controls','Shared','Field, TextInput, PasswordInput, Textarea, Select, Checkbox, RadioGroup, DateInput and NumberInput with labels, help text, error text and required marks wired for screen readers. Every form in the app uses these.','As any user I fill in forms that behave the same everywhere and tell me clearly what is wrong.','UI kit','dev3',2,false,array['U-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (forms)']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/Field.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/TextInput.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/Select.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/RadioGroup.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/controls.test.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Each control has a test with Testing Library (label, error, disabled)','axe passes on the kit page','Keyboard only: every control reachable and usable']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/Field.tsx and the controls; errors linked with aria-describedby; focus moves to the first error on submit','Works with plain React state and with Zod error maps from contracts']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['How should a Zod error from the API land on the right field?','What is the smallest API that covers all controls?','Which controls need a mobile-specific behaviour?']::text[],2532),
('U-03','Feedback components: dialog, toast, notices, states','Shared','Dialog (focus trap, Escape, return focus), ConfirmDialog, Toast, Notice (info, warning, error), EmptyState, ErrorState with Try again and request id, and Skeleton for loading. These make the loading, empty and error states easy for everyone.','As any user I always know what is happening: loading, nothing here yet, or something went wrong and what to do.','UI kit','dev3',3,false,array['U-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/Dialog.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/ErrorState.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/feedback.test.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Dialog traps focus and returns it on close (test)','Toasts are announced by screen readers','ErrorState shows the request id for support']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/Dialog.tsx, ConfirmDialog.tsx, Toast.tsx, Notice.tsx, EmptyState.tsx, ErrorState.tsx, Skeleton.tsx','ErrorState reads the API error shape (code, message, requestId)']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Every screen has loading, empty and error states','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['When is a toast enough and when must it be a notice on the page?','What should every ErrorState offer besides "Try again"?','How do you stop two dialogs opening at once?']::text[],3533),
('U-04','Display components: stage rail, chips, tabs, tables','Shared','StageRail final (done tick, current highlight, later muted, Phase 2 locked), StatusChip and DueChip (overdue, today, this week), Tabs that hide tabs a role cannot use, Card, DataTable with sorting and an accessible scatter chart wrapper used by Results.','As any user I read status, stage and due dates the same way on every screen.','UI kit','dev3',3,false,array['U-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/prototype/index.html (stage rail, chips)','docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §15.4']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/StageRail.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/DueChip.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/Tabs.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/DataTable.tsx','frontend/src/components/ui/display.test.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['StageRail shows all seven stages with Prove, Pilot and Scale locked','DueChip computes from a date and today in the user''s time zone (tests)','DataTable is usable by keyboard and screen reader']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['frontend/src/components/ui/StageRail.tsx, StatusChip.tsx, DueChip.tsx, Tabs.tsx, Card.tsx, DataTable.tsx, ScatterChart.tsx','Stage names and order from contracts/src/stages.ts']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['How does a chip carry meaning without colour alone?','What does Tabs do when the current tab is hidden for this role?','Which chart needs a table alternative?']::text[],3534),
('U-05','Accessibility checks in every test run','Shared','Add axe to component tests and a helper every developer calls in their page tests, plus a keyboard walk-through checklist. From week 4 a screen with a serious axe issue fails pnpm verify.','As a user who relies on a keyboard or screen reader I can use every screen, because the build stops anything that breaks it.','UI kit','dev3',4,false,array['U-02','U-03','U-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/SPEC.md NFR (WCAG 2.1 AA)']::text[],array['frontend/src/test/a11y.ts','frontend/eslint.config.js','docs/ui/ACCESSIBILITY.md']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Every UI kit component test calls the helper','A deliberate missing label fails the test','The helper runs in pnpm verify']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['frontend/src/test/a11y.ts: expectNoA11yViolations(container)','Lint rules from eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y on','docs/ui/ACCESSIBILITY.md: the keyboard checklist and common fixes']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['Which axe rules are false positives here and why?','How will you get the other three to use the helper without nagging?','What can axe not catch, and how does the checklist cover it?']::text[],4535),
('F-01','Worker and job queue','Shared','A second process (backend/src/worker.ts) runs background jobs from a Postgres-backed queue (pg-boss): send email, daily reminders, build exports. Jobs retry with back-off and end in a failed list you can see. The API never sends mail itself.','As the team we run slow or failing work in the background with retries, so that screens stay fast and nothing is lost.','Platform','dev4',2,true,array['S-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §1, §4 (platform)']::text[],array['backend/src/worker.ts','backend/src/platform/jobs.ts','backend/src/platform/jobs.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A job enqueued in a rolled-back transaction never runs','A failing job retries 3 times with back-off then lands in failed','Job payloads never contain emails or free text']::text[],array['backend/src/worker.ts and backend/src/platform/jobs.ts: enqueue(name, payload) in the caller''s transaction, register(name, handler)','Payloads validated by Zod; ids only, never personal data','In-process stub with the same interface merged in week 2 for the other three','pnpm worker script; health log line every minute']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Other modules are used only through their index.ts']::text[],array['Why enqueue in the same transaction as the change?','What happens to jobs if the worker is down for an hour?','How do other developers test their jobs without running the worker?']::text[],2546),
('F-02','Mail adapter and email templates','Shared','One mail adapter sends through SMTP: Mailpit locally, a hosted SMTP provider later (only config changes). Plain, accessible templates for verify email, reset password, invite, reminder and the customer follow-up. Sending always goes through the send-email job.','As any user I get clear, safe emails from the app, and in development every email lands in Mailpit.','Platform','dev4',3,true,array['F-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['GUARDRAILS.md (external services)','README.md (local services)']::text[],array['backend/src/platform/mail.ts','backend/src/platform/mail-templates/*','backend/src/platform/mail.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['All five templates render with invented data and arrive in Mailpit','A link in an email is always to APP_ORIGIN','Mail bodies and recipient emails never appear in logs']::text[],array['backend/src/platform/mail.ts with nodemailer; templates in backend/src/platform/mail-templates/*','send-email job; message id and status stored; no body in logs','Config: SMTP host, port, user, password from env only; refuses to start in production without TLS']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts','Plain words, verb and object on buttons, role titles only, no em dashes']::text[],array['Plain text, HTML or both, and why?','How do you stop an email being sent twice when a job retries?','What must change to switch provider later?']::text[],3547),
('F-03','File storage adapter','Shared','An S3-compatible storage adapter (MinIO locally) for claim sources and exports: upload with size and type limits, download through short-lived signed links, files private by default and scoped to workspace and client.','As a Research analyst or consultant I attach and download files safely, so that sources and exports are kept but never public.','Platform','dev4',4,false,array['S-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7']::text[],array['backend/src/platform/storage.ts','backend/src/platform/storage.test.ts']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A file over 10 MB or of a refused type is rejected','A signed link stops working after 5 minutes','A member of another workspace cannot get a link to a file']::text[],array['backend/src/platform/storage.ts: put, getSignedUrl, delete; keys workspace/client/kind/uuid','Allowed types and 10 MB limit; content type checked from the bytes, not the name','Signed links valid for 5 minutes']::text[],array['A FileUpload control added to the UI kit by agreement with Developer 3, or a simple input in the feature']::text[],array['404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','Every input goes through the contract schema; unknown fields are rejected with 400','No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs']::text[],array['Why check the type from the bytes?','Who may delete a file and what happens to references?','How is MinIO set up in docker-compose and in CI?']::text[],4548),
('F-04','End-to-end test harness','Shared','Playwright in e2e/ with a seeded database, a sign-in helper per role, a participant join helper and a Mailpit helper to read links. One smoke journey (register, onboard as lead, create client) runs in CI on every merge request. Every stage adds its own journey on top.','As a developer I write a full journey test for my stage in minutes, so that integration problems show up the day they happen.','Platform','dev4',3,true,array['S-4']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/PHASE1_PLAN.md §10.3 (journey test)']::text[],array['e2e/playwright.config.ts','e2e/fixtures.ts','e2e/specs/smoke.spec.ts','docs/testing/E2E.md']::text[],array[]::text[],array['The smoke journey passes three runs in a row locally and in CI','Helpers work for all four roles and a participant','A failing test keeps a trace and screenshot as a CI artifact']::text[],array['Test seed command that resets the database to a known state']::text[],array['e2e/fixtures.ts: signInAs(role), joinAsPod(code), readMail(to)','e2e/specs/smoke.spec.ts','docs/testing/E2E.md: how to add your stage journey']::text[],array['Screens pass axe and work by keyboard only']::text[],array['How do you keep end-to-end tests fast and not flaky?','Which journeys must every stage owner write?','What data does each journey need, and who owns the seed?']::text[],3549),
('F-05','CI security scans and merge rules','Shared','Harden the GitLab pipeline: Semgrep, gitleaks, OSV-Scanner and pnpm audit on every merge request, a container scan (Trivy) on the image, protected main with one approval from CODEOWNERS and a green pipeline. Findings at high or medium fail the pipeline.','As the team we cannot merge a leaked secret or a known vulnerable package by accident.','Platform','dev4',4,false,array['F-04']::text[],array[]::text[],array['GUARDRAILS.md','.gitlab-ci.yml','CODEOWNERS']::text[],array['.gitlab-ci.yml','tools/semgrep/*','docs/security/SCANS.md']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A commit with a fake key (test fixture) is blocked by gitleaks','A known vulnerable package version fails the pipeline','The full pipeline runs under 15 minutes']::text[],array['.gitlab-ci.yml stages: install, verify, test, e2e, security, build','Semgrep rules for this codebase in tools/semgrep/: raw SQL outside repo.ts, dangerouslySetInnerHTML, process.env outside config.ts']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Routes only through defineRoute with a contract and a permission','Database access only in repo.ts, every query scoped by workspaceId']::text[],array['Which findings may be accepted, by whom, and where is that recorded?','How do you keep CI fast as tests grow?','Which GitLab features are free on our plan, and which need a free tool instead?']::text[],4540),
('F-06','Container build and full local stack','Shared','A small, non-root Docker image for the backend (API and worker from one image), the frontend built as static files, and a compose profile that runs the whole app like production. Health and ready endpoints show database and queue status.','As the team we can run the whole app exactly as it will be hosted, so that hosting later is a config change.','Platform','dev4',5,false,array['F-01']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §9','docs/hosting (later)']::text[],array['backend/Dockerfile','frontend/Dockerfile','docker-compose.yml']::text[],array['GET /api/health','GET /api/ready']::text[],array['docker compose --profile full up runs the smoke journey','The image runs as a non-root user and has no shell tools it does not need','Ready fails when the database is down']::text[],array['backend/Dockerfile multi-stage, node 22 slim, non-root user, no dev dependencies','GET /api/health and GET /api/ready (database and queue check)','docker-compose.yml profile "full": api, worker, web (static), Postgres, Mailpit, MinIO']::text[],array['frontend build served by a tiny static server or nginx with the same security headers']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs']::text[],array['How do migrations run on deploy, and who runs them?','Which secrets does the image need, and how do they arrive?','How big is the image, and what makes it smaller?']::text[],5541),
('F-07','Logs, request ids and error tracking','Shared','Structured logs with request id, user id and workspace id (no personal data), the request id returned in every error, and error tracking with a free hosted service in a way that scrubs personal data before sending. Slow requests over 500 ms are logged.','As a developer I can find what went wrong for a user from the request id they read off the error screen.','Platform','dev4',6,false,array['F-06']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7']::text[],array['backend/src/core/logger.ts','backend/src/platform/errors.ts','frontend/src/app/ErrorBoundary.tsx']::text[],array[]::text[],array['A test proves cookies, passwords, tokens and emails are redacted','An error screen shows a request id that is in the logs','Error tracking is off unless its key is set']::text[],array['Logger settings in backend/src/core/logger.ts extended; error tracking adapter in backend/src/platform/errors.ts with scrubbing','Frontend error boundary sends errors with the request id']::text[],array['Error boundary using ErrorState from the UI kit']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs','Customer free text only in the pii schema; no personal names in events, logs or drafts']::text[],array['What must never leave the server in an error report?','How long are logs kept, and where?','Which signals tell you the app is slow for 40 users?']::text[],6542),
('F-08','Load test for 40 people at once','Shared','A k6 script that plays 40 concurrent users (leads, team, consultant and pods in a live session) for 15 minutes on the full stack. Targets: 95% of API calls under 300 ms, no errors, live updates within 2 seconds. Fix or report what fails.','As the team we know the app holds up on session day with everyone using it at once.','Platform','dev4',8,false,array['F-06']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/blueprint/SPEC.md NFR (performance)']::text[],array['load/k6/session-day.js','docs/perf/RESULTS.md']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Targets met on a laptop-sized container, or each miss has an issue with the cause','No database connection pool exhaustion','Open server-sent event connections are cleaned up']::text[],array['load/k6/session-day.js with seeded data; results written to docs/perf/RESULTS.md','Database indexes checked with EXPLAIN for the top 10 queries']::text[],array['None']::text[],array['Database access only in repo.ts, every query scoped by workspaceId']::text[],array['What does a realistic session-day traffic mix look like?','Which query will be the first to hurt?','How do you load-test the stream connections?']::text[],8543),
('F-09','Security baseline on the release candidate','Shared','Run a ZAP baseline scan against the full stack, check headers, cookies and the content security policy, and fix every high and medium finding with the owner of that code. Record the results.','As the team we ship the release candidate with no known high or medium security issue.','Platform','dev4',9,false,array['F-05']::text[],array[]::text[],array['GUARDRAILS.md','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7']::text[],array['docs/security/FINDINGS.md','.gitlab-ci.yml (zap job)']::text[],array[]::text[],array['No high or medium finding open','No secret in the Git history','docs/security/FINDINGS.md lists every finding and its fix or acceptance']::text[],array['ZAP baseline in CI on the full compose stack; header and cookie checks as tests']::text[],array['Content security policy has no unsafe-inline for scripts']::text[],array['No secrets, tokens, passwords or emails in logs']::text[],array['Which findings are real for a single-page app with cookie sessions?','Who decides to accept a low finding?','What should be re-checked after every future release?']::text[],9544),
('X-1','Integration checkpoint 1 (27 Nov)','Finish','All four developers merge to main by Friday noon, then run the app together for two hours and check what this checkpoint must show. The owner of this task runs the session, keeps the notes in docs/checkpoints/IC1.md and makes sure every gap has an owner and a date.','As the team we join our work every two weeks, so that the four stages fit together long before the end.','Integration','dev1',2,true,array['K-1']::text[],array[]::text[],array['docs/APP_FLOW.md','docs/ARCHITECTURE.md','README.md (daily routine)']::text[],array['docs/checkpoints/IC1.md']::text[],array[]::text[],array['Every prototype screen is covered by at least one frozen contract','Every stub route answers 501 with the frozen schema','Tag contracts-v1; from now on a contract change is its own merge request','Tag ic1 on main','docs/checkpoints/IC1.md lists findings with an owner and a date']::text[],array['Every merged stub that should now be real is removed (search for "stub" in backend/src/modules)','pnpm verify and the end-to-end smoke journey pass on the tag']::text[],array['Walk the screens listed below on a shared screen, as each role']::text[],array['Routes only through defineRoute with a contract and a permission','404 for a workspace you are not in, or a client card you cannot see','403 for a role without the permission, and nothing is written']::text[],array['Which contract clashes did the review find, and how were they settled?','Which screens have no contract yet?']::text[],2615),
